1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,920
Pyramids. Cleopatra.
The Suez Canal.

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:05,205
All thanks to one
river: the Nile.

3
00:00:05,245 --> 00:00:08,685
Around 3100 BC,
Upper and Lower Egypt

4
00:00:08,725 --> 00:00:10,554
unite under one king.

5
00:00:10,594 --> 00:00:14,614
Around 2560 BC, the
Great Pyramid rises,

6
00:00:14,654 --> 00:00:18,320
the world's tallest structure
for nearly 4,000 years.

7
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:22,440
In 1279 BC, Ramesses
II takes the throne,

8
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:25,364
and cuts giant
temples into cliffs.

9
00:00:25,404 --> 00:00:29,524
In 332 BC, Alexander
the Great arrives.

10
00:00:29,564 --> 00:00:31,882
After Cleopatra,
Rome takes over.

11
00:00:31,922 --> 00:00:34,462
In 641, Arab
armies bring Islam,

12
00:00:34,502 --> 00:00:37,633
and Cairo grows into
a great capital.

13
00:00:37,673 --> 00:00:41,553
In 1869, Egypt opens
the Suez Canal,

14
00:00:41,593 --> 00:00:44,443
linking the Mediterranean
to the Red Sea.

15
00:00:44,483 --> 00:00:48,143
In 1952, a revolution
ends the monarchy,

16
00:00:48,183 --> 00:00:51,108
and the Aswan High Dam
later tames the Nile.

17
00:00:51,148 --> 00:00:54,028
Today, over 100 million
people live here,

18
00:00:54,068 --> 00:00:55,877
most of them along the Nile.

19
00:00:55,917 --> 00:00:59,700
Which country should
we print next?

